### Poplar
From the initial briefing, I knew that Poplar finds wearing party hats embarrassing, that Poplar’s favourite animal is the otter, and that Poplar spends spare time pressing flowers. During the session, Poplar shared the clue that Mara had night shift or medicine, but not both, and later shared the recovered clue that geology came earlier than Lab. Poplar also sent shorthand-ledger and audit notes; I did not conclude any additional personal facts from those notes. By the end, Poplar had independently derived the same solution as the rest of us.

### Pine
From the initial briefing, I knew that Pine’s go-to snack is roasted almonds, that Pine is usually free late on Friday evenings, and that Pine loves the smell of old books. During the session, Pine shared Lena’s Comms-or-robotics clue and the recovered clue that Mara had Comms or dusk, but not both. Pine also caught an invalid provisional assignment in which the Lab holder and chemistry specialist were the same person. By the end, Pine had solved and submitted the agreed assignment.

### Birch
From the initial briefing, I knew that Birch loves bluegrass and has been wanting a good pair of binoculars. During the session, Birch shared that Observatory came earlier than medicine and later shared that Hydroponics did not have night shift. Near the end, Birch briefly thought the combined clues were inconsistent, then acknowledged an overlooked possibility and confirmed and submitted our agreed solution.

### Juniper
From the initial briefing, I knew that Juniper has been wanting a book of crosswords, that Juniper’s favourite cake is cheesecake, and that Juniper’s favourite drink is espresso. During the session, Juniper shared Ines’s dawn-or-geology clue and later shared Kofi’s dusk-or-robotics clue. Juniper independently derived the final solution and its uniqueness, submitted it, and confirmed that all five of us had reached the same answer.

### Hornbeam
From the initial briefing, I knew that Hornbeam is allergic to shellfish. Hornbeam was not working on this puzzle, and I learned nothing further about Hornbeam during the session.

### Acacia
From the initial briefing, I knew that Acacia finds wearing party hats embarrassing. Acacia was not working on this puzzle, and I learned nothing further about Acacia during the session.

### Baobab
From the initial briefing, I knew that Baobab’s favourite kind of film is westerns and that Baobab’s favourite colour is amber. Baobab was not working on this puzzle, and I learned nothing further about Baobab during the session.

### Fig
From the initial briefing, I knew that Fig’s favourite drink is espresso. Fig was not working on this puzzle. Poplar mentioned Fig’s initial in a ledger-notation message, but I did not learn any additional personal fact about Fig from it.

